<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia says copter service contract A$125 mln.</title>
<headline>Australia says copter service contract A$125 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government on Thursday valued a support contract for its new Navy helicopters deal at A$125 million over 13 years.</p>
<p>&quot;The support contract is worth A$125 million,&quot; defence industry minister Browyn Bishop told parliament.</p>
<p>The in-serice contract would provide 13 years of support services for 11 helicopters for the Royal Australian Navy.</p>
<p>Australian defence minister Ian McLachlan said earlier that Kaman Aerospace International, a unit of Kaman Corp, had signed a A$660 million deal to provide the 11 Seasprte SH-2G helicopters to the Royal Australian Navy.  </p>
<p>The services contract is in addition to the A$660 million deal with Kaman.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
